    "slot_value": "Analysts must record which requirement supports which goal, and which policy or legal source justified that goal or requirement; the workbench should also represent overlaps, dependencies, and derived connections so reviewers can see the reasoning, not just the final statement. It should capture the specific source policy reference, the exact part of the policy that justifies the goal, a short rationale explaining the connection, and who made the trace and when, so reviewers can see whether it was added deliberately and by whom. The tool should allow traces supported by several policies together or indirect links through a requirement or scenario, as long as the relationship is still explainable. Overlapping traces should be visible rather than hidden under a single path, with all relevant links shown when an item belongs to multiple paths and any designated primary link made clear. When a requirement traces back to a source policy, the trace should preserve intermediate goals or policy versions when that helps explain the justification path, while keeping the direct policy link prominent so people can quickly get to the authoritative source.",
